MongoDB dump with behavioral and modeling data.

# Requirements

* MongoDB >= 3.2.8

# Usage

    cat dump.tar.gz.parta* > dump.tar.gz
    tar -xzvf dump.tar.gz
    mongorestore dump/

# Collections

- `games`: game and level descriptions
- `subjects`: subjects; id field is `subj_id`; no demographic/identifying data
- `runs`: scanner runs; id field is `run_id` (starting from 1; 0 is the practice run outside the scanner)
- `plays`: episodes of gameplay, including all keypresses and game states
- `regressors`: EMPA regressors, derived from `plays` with EMPA
- `dqn_regressors_25M`: DDQN regressors, derived from `plays` with DDQN
- `plays_post`: visual confound regressors, derived from `plays` after some post processing
- `sim_results`: result from generative play for EMPA and DDQN

# Version history of the dump

In versions 1.0.0 and 1.0.1, the `regressors` collection was incomplete. It held 5,241 of
6,652 plays: subject 2 had none, and most other subjects were missing some. It came from a
database snapshot taken partway through the final EMPA replay batch in July 2021. Version
1.0.2 replaces `regressors.bson` with the complete collection. The 5,241 documents that were
already there are unchanged, byte for byte. All other collections are identical to 1.0.1.

# GLM inputs

`glm_inputs.tar.gz` contains the exact per-run SPM designs (GLMs 102–106) and cached EMPA
regressors used for the theory-update analyses in the paper. See `glm_inputs/README.md`
inside the archive for details. One note: for subject 2, run 1, the published analyses used
an earlier EMPA replay than the one stored in the Mongo dump. Only `glm_inputs.tar.gz` has
that earlier replay.

    tar -xzvf glm_inputs.tar.gz
